# API

## Mục tiêu

API (Application Programming Interface) là cửa ngõ chính để các hệ thống giao tiếp với nhau và với clients. Một API được thiết kế tốt không chỉ cung cấp functionality mà còn đảm bảo developer experience tuyệt vời, dễ dàng mở rộng, và có khả năng bảo trì lâu dài. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, API design principles đóng vai trò quan trọng trong việc tạo ra các dịch vụ có thể tích hợp liền mạch, hỗ trợ nhiều clients, và evolve theo thời gian mà không gây ra breaking changes cho existing consumers.

Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc thiết kế APIs nhất quán, an toàn, và có hiệu suất cao. Từ việc chọn đúng architectural style (REST, GraphQL, gRPC), đến việc implement proper error handling, versioning, và documentation, tất cả đều được cover chi tiết trong rule này.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. API First Development**

Thiết kế API contract trước khi implement. Sử dụng OpenAPI/Swagger hoặc AsyncAPI để define contracts. Review contracts với stakeholders trước khi coding. Contracts become documentation và contract tests. API-first giúp parallel development giữa teams.

**2. Consistent Naming Conventions**

Sử dụng consistent naming cho resources, actions, và parameters. RESTful URLs nên use nouns không phải verbs. Use kebab-case cho multi-word paths. Use camelCase cho query parameters. Consistent naming improves discoverability và reduces cognitive load.

**3. Proper HTTP Method Usage**

GET cho resource retrieval. POST cho resource creation. PUT cho full resource update. PATCH cho partial updates. DELETE cho resource removal. Response codes phản ánh operation result. Improper method usage leads to confusion và bugs.

**4. Pagination for Large Datasets**

Tất cả list endpoints phải support pagination. Use cursor-based pagination cho large datasets. Offset-based acceptable cho small, stable datasets. Return pagination metadata (total, page, limit). Allow clients to specify page size within limits.

**5. Versioning Strategy**

Version APIs để enable evolution without breaking clients. URL versioning (/v1/users) là simplest approach. Header versioning offers cleaner URLs nhưng less discoverable. Maintain multiple versions simultaneously. Deprecate old versions with clear timeline.

**6. Error Response Standards**

Use standard error response format across all APIs. Include error code, message, và details. Use appropriate HTTP status codes. Include request ID for debugging. Error responses must be consistent format.

**7. Rate Limiting và Throttling**

Implement rate limiting để protect APIs from abuse. Return rate limit headers (X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining). Use standard HTTP 429 for rate limit exceeded. Implement different limits for different tiers. Consider client-specific limits.

**8. Security Best Practices**

Authenticate all API requests. Authorize based on permissions. Validate all inputs. Sanitize outputs. Use HTTPS everywhere. Implement CORS properly. Rotate API keys regularly.

**9. Documentation First**

Documentation is not afterthought - it's product. Use OpenAPI/Swagger for REST docs. Include request/response examples. Document error codes và meanings. Keep docs in sync with implementation. Interactive documentation improves developer experience.

**10. API Monitoring và Analytics**

Track API usage patterns. Monitor response times và error rates. Track which endpoints are popular. Analyze client behavior. Use analytics to guide API evolution.

## Checklist

- [ ] API contract defined in OpenAPI format
- [ ] Consistent naming conventions established
- [ ] HTTP methods used correctly
- [ ] Pagination implemented for list endpoints
- [ ] Versioning strategy defined và implemented
- [ ] Error responses standardized
- [ ] Rate limiting configured
- [ ] Authentication và authorization implemented
- [ ] Documentation complete và accurate
- [ ] Monitoring và analytics setup
- [ ] API tests written
- [ ] Breaking changes review performed

## Anti Pattern

**1. Chatty APIs**

Multiple round trips needed to complete simple operations. Force clients to make many requests. Solution: Use bulk endpoints, composite resources, và field selection.

**2. Exposing Database Schema**

Database schema directly exposed as API. Tight coupling between DB và API. Schema changes break clients. Solution: Create separate API models from database models.

**3. No Error Standards**

Different error formats across endpoints. Inconsistent HTTP status codes. Missing error details. Solution: Standardize error response format system-wide.

**4. Versioning After the Fact**

API released without versioning. Changes require breaking existing clients. Solution: Version from day one. Plan for evolution.

**5. Ignoring Backwards Compatibility**

Making breaking changes without notice. No deprecation policy. Clients suddenly break. Solution: Follow semver principles. Maintain backwards compatibility. Provide migration guides.

## Best Practice

**1. API Design with OpenAPI**

```yaml
openapi: 3.0.0
info:
  title: User Management API
  version: 1.0.0
  description: API for managing users in the system

servers:
  - url: https://api.example.com/v1
    description: Production server
  - url: https://staging-api.example.com/v1
    description: Staging server

paths:
  /users:
    get:
      summary: List users
      description: Returns a paginated list of users
      parameters:
        - name: page
          in: query
          schema:
            type: integer
            default: 1
        - name: limit
          in: query
          schema:
            type: integer
            default: 20
            maximum: 100
        - name: search
          in: query
          schema:
            type: string
      responses:
        '200':
          description: Successful response
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/UserListResponse'
        '400':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'
        '401':
          $ref: '#/components/responses/Unauthorized'

components:
  schemas:
    User:
      type: object
      properties:
        id:
          type: string
          format: uuid
        email:
          type: string
          format: email
        name:
          type: string
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
    UserListResponse:
      type: object
      properties:
        data:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'
        pagination:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Pagination'
  responses:
    BadRequest:
      description: Bad request
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'
```

**2. GraphQL Schema Design**

```graphql
type Query {
  user(id: ID!): User
  users(
    page: Int = 1
    limit: Int = 20
    search: String
    sortBy: UserSortField = CREATED_AT
    sortOrder: SortOrder = DESC
  ): UserConnection!
}

type Mutation {
  createUser(input: CreateUserInput!): CreateUserPayload!
  updateUser(id: ID!, input: UpdateUserInput!): UpdateUserPayload!
  deleteUser(id: ID!): DeleteUserPayload!
}

type User {
  id: ID!
  email: String!
  name: String!
  profile: UserProfile
  roles: [Role!]!
  createdAt: DateTime!
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

type UserConnection {
  edges: [UserEdge!]!
  pageInfo: PageInfo!
  totalCount: Int!
}

type UserEdge {
  node: User!
  cursor: String!
}

type PageInfo {
  hasNextPage: Boolean!
  hasPreviousPage: Boolean!
  startCursor: String
  endCursor: String
}

input CreateUserInput {
  email: String!
  name: String!
  password: String!
  roleIds: [ID!]!
}

input UpdateUserInput {
  email: String
  name: String
  profile: UpdateProfileInput
}
```

**3. API Error Handling**

```typescript
// Standard error response format
interface ApiError {
  code: string;
  message: string;
  details?: Record<string, any>;
  requestId: string;
  timestamp: string;
  helpUrl?: string;
}

// Error codes enumeration
enum ErrorCode {
  VALIDATION_ERROR = 'VALIDATION_ERROR',
  NOT_FOUND = 'NOT_FOUND',
  UNAUTHORIZED = 'UNAUTHORIZED',
  FORBIDDEN = 'FORBIDDEN',
  RATE_LIMITED = 'RATE_LIMITED',
  INTERNAL_ERROR = 'INTERNAL_ERROR',
  SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE = 'SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE'
}

// Error handler middleware
class ApiErrorHandler {
  handle(error: Error, request: Request, response: Response, next: NextFunction) {
    const requestId = request.headers['x-request-id'] || generateRequestId();
    
    if (error instanceof ValidationError) {
      return response.status(400).json({
        code: ErrorCode.VALIDATION_ERROR,
        message: 'Validation failed',
        details: error.details,
        requestId,
        timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
      });
    }
    
    if (error instanceof NotFoundError) {
      return response.status(404).json({
        code: ErrorCode.NOT_FOUND,
        message: error.message,
        requestId,
        timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
      });
    }
    
    if (error instanceof UnauthorizedError) {
      return response.status(401).json({
        code: ErrorCode.UNAUTHORIZED,
        message: 'Authentication required',
        requestId,
        timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
      });
    }
    
    // Log unexpected errors
    logger.error('Unexpected error', { error, requestId });
    
    return response.status(500).json({
      code: ErrorCode.INTERNAL_ERROR,
      message: 'An unexpected error occurred',
      requestId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      helpUrl: 'https://docs.example.com/errors'
    });
  }
}
```

**4. Rate Limiting Implementation**

```typescript
class RateLimiter {
  constructor(
    private redis: Redis,
    private config: RateLimitConfig
  ) {}
  
  async checkLimit(
    identifier: string,
    endpoint: string
  ): Promise<RateLimitResult> {
    const key = `ratelimit:${endpoint}:${identifier}`;
    const now = Date.now();
    const windowStart = now - this.config.windowMs;
    
    // Remove old entries
    await this.redis.zremrangebyscore(key, 0, windowStart);
    
    // Count current requests
    const count = await this.redis.zcard(key);
    
    if (count >= this.config.maxRequests) {
      const oldest = await this.redis.zrange(key, 0, 0, 'WITHSCORES');
      const retryAfter = oldest.length > 1 
        ? Math.ceil((parseInt(oldest[1]) + this.config.windowMs - now) / 1000)
        : this.config.windowMs / 1000;
      
      return {
        allowed: false,
        remaining: 0,
        limit: this.config.maxRequests,
        reset: Math.ceil((now + this.config.windowMs) / 1000),
        retryAfter
      };
    }
    
    // Add current request
    await this.redis.zadd(key, now, `${now}:${Math.random()}`);
    await this.redis.expire(key, Math.ceil(this.config.windowMs / 1000));
    
    return {
      allowed: true,
      remaining: this.config.maxRequests - count - 1,
      limit: this.config.maxRequests,
      reset: Math.ceil((now + this.config.windowMs) / 1000),
      retryAfter: 0
    };
  }
}

// Rate limit middleware
async function rateLimitMiddleware(
  request: Request,
  response: Response,
  next: NextFunction
) {
  const identifier = getClientIdentifier(request);
  const endpoint = request.path;
  
  const result = await rateLimiter.checkLimit(identifier, endpoint);
  
  response.setHeader('X-RateLimit-Limit', result.limit);
  response.setHeader('X-RateLimit-Remaining', result.remaining);
  response.setHeader('X-RateLimit-Reset', result.reset);
  
  if (!result.allowed) {
    response.setHeader('Retry-After', result.retryAfter);
    return response.status(429).json({
      code: 'RATE_LIMITED',
      message: 'Too many requests',
      retryAfter: result.retryAfter
    });
  }
  
  next();
}
```

**5. API Versioning**

```typescript
// Version extraction middleware
class ApiVersionMiddleware {
  extractVersion(request: Request): string {
    // Check URL path first
    const pathMatch = request.path.match(/^\/v(\d+)/);
    if (pathMatch) {
      return `v${pathMatch[1]}`;
    }
    
    // Check header
    const headerVersion = request.headers['api-version'];
    if (headerVersion) {
      return `v${headerVersion}`;
    }
    
    return 'v1'; // Default version
  }
  
  routeToVersionHandler(
    request: Request,
    response: Response,
    next: NextFunction
  ) {
    const version = this.extractVersion(request);
    const handlerKey = `${request.method}:${request.path}:${version}`;
    
    const handler = this.versionedHandlers.get(handlerKey);
    if (handler) {
      return handler(request, response, next);
    }
    
    // Fallback to default version
    const defaultHandler = this.versionedHandlers.get(
      `${request.method}:${request.path}:default`
    );
    
    if (defaultHandler) {
      return defaultHandler(request, response, next);
    }
    
    next();
  }
}

// Deprecation handling
class DeprecationHandler {
  async checkDeprecation(
    request: Request
  ): Promise<void> {
    const version = this.extractVersion(request);
    const deprecation = await this.deprecationStore.get(version);
    
    if (deprecation) {
      response.setHeader('Deprecation', 'true');
      response.setHeader(
        'Sunset',
        new Date(deprecation.sunsetDate).toUTCString()
      );
      response.setHeader(
        'Link',
        `<${deprecation.deprecatedUrl}>; rel="deprecation"`
      );
    }
  }
}
```

## Workflow

**Phase 1: Requirements Gathering**

Thu thập requirements từ stakeholders. Document use cases và workflows. Identify client types và their needs. Define non-functional requirements. Establish success metrics.

**Phase 2: Contract Design**

Design API contract using OpenAPI/AsyncAPI. Review contract with stakeholders. Iterate based on feedback. Get sign-off on contract. This becomes the source of truth.

**Phase 3: Implementation**

Implement according to contract. Write contract tests. Generate mocks from contract. Keep implementation in sync with contract. Regular contract validation.

**Phase 4: Documentation**

Generate interactive documentation. Add examples và tutorials. Document error codes. Keep docs in sync. Publish documentation.

**Phase 5: Testing**

Write integration tests. Perform contract testing. Load test endpoints. Security test the API. Get security review.

**Phase 6: Deployment và Monitoring**

Deploy to staging environment. Smoke test deployed API. Configure monitoring. Set up alerts. Deploy to production.

**Phase 7: Version Management**

Monitor API usage by version. Plan deprecation timeline. Communicate deprecation to clients. Maintain old versions per SLA.

